This page defines the strict interior charged barotropic model and develops its current balance, positive symmetric fluid block, local coupled development, and compact-slice charge compatibility. Its local development is conditional on the inspected CP01 Maxwell-stress identity and CP02 field-strength reduction interfaces; those prerequisite carriers remain drafts and are recorded as unresolved in the batch evidence. No shocks, vacuum boundaries, finite-conductivity law, global existence, or empirical validation are asserted.
